{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nVanya has a scales for weighing loads and weights of masses w0,\u2009w1,\u2009w2,\u2009...,\u2009w100 grams where w is some integer not less than 2 (exactly one weight of each nominal value). Vanya wonders whether he can weight an item with mass m using the given weights, if the weights can be put on both pans of the scales. Formally speaking, your task is to determine whether it is possible to place an item of mass m and some weights on the left pan of the scales, and some weights on the right pan of the scales so that the pans of the scales were in balance.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 7 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CodeForce308C {\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = in.readLine().trim();\n        String[] parts = line.split(\" +\");\n        long w = Long.parseLong(parts[0]);\n        long m = Long.parseLong(parts[1]);\n        \n        if (w == 2) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        List<Long> combination = new ArrayList<>();\n        combination.add(0L);\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i <= 100; i++) {\n            long power = 1;\n            try {\n                power = Math.multiplyExact(1L, (long) Math.pow(w, i));\n            } catch (ArithmeticException e) {\n                break;\n            }\n            if (power > (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE) {\n                break;\n            }\n            \n            int size = combination.size();\n            for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\n                long sum = combination.get(j) + power;\n                if (sum <= (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE) {\n                    combination.add(sum);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        Collections.sort(combination);\n        \n        if (Collections.binarySearch(combination, m) >= 0) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        for (Long element : combination) {\n            if (element + m <= (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE && \n                Collections.binarySearch(combination, element + m) >= 0) {\n                System.out.println(\"YES\");\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(\"NO\");\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CodeForce308C {\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = in.readLine().trim();\n        String[] parts = line.split(\" +\");\n        long w = Long.parseLong(parts[0]);\n        long m = Long.parseLong(parts[1]);\n        \n        // Special case: if w = 2, any mass can be balanced\n        if (w == 2) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // We'll use a set to store all possible combinations\n        Set<Long> combinations = new HashSet<>();\n        combinations.add(0L);\n        \n        // Generate all possible sums using weights w^0, w^1, ..., w^100\n        // Each weight can be placed on left pan (-1), right pan (+1), or not used (0)\n        // So we need to check if m can be represented as sum of coefficients * w^i where coefficients are -1, 0, or 1\n        // This is equivalent to checking if m can be balanced\n        \n        // Instead of generating all combinations explicitly (which could be huge),\n        // we use a different approach: simulate the balance equation\n        \n        // The key insight: we can represent the problem as finding coefficients c_i in {-1, 0, 1} such that\n        // sum(c_i * w^i) = m\n        // This is equivalent to checking if m can be represented in balanced ternary-like system with base w\n        \n        // Algorithm: process m digit by digit in base w\n        // At each step, m % w should be 0, 1, or w-1 (which corresponds to -1 in balanced representation)\n        // If m % w == 0, then current digit is 0\n        // If m % w == 1, then current digit is 1 (weight on right pan)\n        // If m % w == w-1, then current digit is -1 (weight on left pan with the item)\n        // Otherwise, it's impossible\n        \n        boolean possible = true;\n        while (m > 0) {\n            long remainder = m % w;\n            if (remainder == 0) {\n                // No weight needed at this position\n                m = m / w;\n            } else if (remainder == 1) {\n                // Put weight w^i on right pan\n                m = (m - 1) / w;\n            } else if (remainder == w - 1) {\n                // Put weight w^i on left pan (with the item)\n                m = (m + 1) / w;\n            } else {\n                possible = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(possible ? \"YES\" : \"NO\");\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.932505594799295e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.782778655178845e-05, -3.0278701160568744e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -9.65590606938349e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0001012035645544529, -1.1444026313256472e-05, -7.986990567587782e-06, -0.0008228015503846109, -0.00020108585886191577, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.006777428206988e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.01251098420470953, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -6.556489552167477e-06, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -9.775113539944869e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0001793938863556832, -1.549708758830093e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.629365427419543e-06, -1.168244216387393e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.4638240878121e-06, -5.960446742392378e-06, -5.960446742392378e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -2.9682672902708873e-05, -5.018585216021165e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.731181277544238e-05, -9.703165414975956e-05, -4.2437604861333966e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.099436753473128e-06, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -7.593343616463244e-05, -3.2543604902457446e-05, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -7.152531907195225e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -8.34461570775602e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07